[start-outcomes] After this part you should be able to
1. explain why a column on the site boundary cannot sit on a pad of its own, and choose between a strap footing and a rectangular or trapezoidal combined footing;
2. find the reactions of a strap footing by statics, size its two footings for the allowable bearing pressure, and draw the shear force and bending moment of the strap;
3. design the strap beam, with its main bars at the top and its links over footing A, and the two footings it ties together;
4. size a pile group from the service load and the pile capacity (number, spacing, cap size and depth), and find the load on each pile under a moment.
